title: "Fix 'move application to bin' errors on macOS using xattr"
---
Fix F***ING macOS errors when you have a homebrew installed application that breaks the verification after an upgrade.

I've installed Headlamp through Homebrew and after an update it wouldn't start anymore. Apparently some signatures were invalidated by the update. You can update the signatures using:

```
xattr -cr /Applications/Headlamp.app
```

And the application will start again.
